.TH ZEX-DOCTOR 1 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-doctor \- audit and repair the Zainium package system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elevate zex doctor
.RI [ \-\-fix ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex doctor
performs a comprehensive health audit of the Zainium package system:
.TP
\(bu
Registry consistency \(em every receipt in
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/installed/
has all declared files present on disk.
.TP
\(bu
Orphaned files \(em files under
.I /overlayer/zexlib/union/
not tracked by any receipt.
.TP
\(bu
Broken symlinks \(em symlinks created by installed packages that
now point to nonexistent targets.
.TP
\(bu
Syshub integrity \(em key paths in
.I /overlayer/syshub/
exist and are not corrupted.
.TP
\(bu
glibc contamination \(em ELF binaries linked against
.I libc.so.6
(which is not present in ZainiumOS).
.TP
\(bu
musl/relibc interpreter correctness \(em dynamic linker paths
point to
.I /overlayer/syshub/x86_64-zainium-linux-musl/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1
or the relibc equivalent.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-fix ,
.B zex doctor
attempts to repair each detected issue automatically. Registry-index
repair fully rebuilds the derived
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/packages.toml
master index from the authoritative per-package receipts in
.IR /overlayer/zexlib/registry/installed/ ,
rather than patching it incrementally, so the fix is correct even if the
index was corrupted or badly out of sync.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Attempt automatic repair of all detected issues.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
System is healthy (or all found issues were repaired with \-\-fix).
.TP
.B 1
Issues found that could not be auto-repaired.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zai-env (1)
